    "reason": "[ev-3ab1e090dc9b] only says source-watcher was \"added to the Flux distribution\". It does not say whether the controller is installed by default or only when chosen as an optional component, or which setting selects it. The surrounding changelog items ([ev-2a1f31a924a0], [ev-ca5d9cebd770]) don't answer this either. So the proposed exposure, every environment upgrading from a version below 2.7.0, can't be confirmed: it would be too broad if the component is opt-in. Missing: an install or upgrade note, or the bootstrap or install manifests, showing whether source-watcher is a default component and, if not, which setting enables it.",
